<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Workers' and Peasants' Red Army</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Red Army was the army of Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, founded by the Bolsheviks in 1918 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leon-trotsky">Leon Trotsky</a> to fight the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>. It conquered the independent republics of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> in 1920–1921 and later drove the German armies back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. It was renamed the Soviet Army in 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-army.jpg" alt="Red Army" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RKKA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soviet_Red_Army_Hammer_and_Sickle.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
